Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: Skip slave timing enable on Lenovo Y700 Gen4

On Lenovo Y700 Gen4, display off/on still leaves the panel blank after
the MDSS hardware-control workaround removes panel initialization
timeouts. Both layer-mixer CRCs are zero despite the absence of display
errors. Skipping the bonded slave's independent timing enable restores
nonzero CRCs and visible output in repeated off/on tests.

Leave timing enable to the bonded master. Keep the slave's software-state
transition, locking, disable path and resource cleanup unchanged; tests
do not require bypassing slave disable or cleanup.

Scope the workaround to Lenovo Y700 Gen4's slave encoder; solo encoders
and other boards retain the existing sequence. This complements rather
than replaces the MDSS hardware-control workaround.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include "disp/msm_disp_snapshot.h"
 #include "msm_dsc_helper.h"
 
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <drm/display/drm_dsc_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_managed.h>
 
@@ -662,7 +663,14 @@ static void dpu_encoder_phys_vid_handle_post_kickoff(
 		trace_dpu_enc_phys_vid_post_kickoff(DRMID(phys_enc->parent),
 				    phys_enc->hw_intf->idx - INTF_0);
 		spin_lock_irqsave(phys_enc->enc_spinlock, lock_flags);
-		phys_enc->hw_intf->ops.enable_timing(phys_enc->hw_intf, 1);
+		/*
+		 * Independently enabling the bonded slave leaves Lenovo Y700
+		 * Gen4 blank after display off/on. Let the master start timing,
+		 * but keep the slave's software-state transition below.
+		 */
+		if (!of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,elden") ||
+		    dpu_encoder_phys_vid_is_master(phys_enc))
+			phys_enc->hw_intf->ops.enable_timing(phys_enc->hw_intf, 1);
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(phys_enc->enc_spinlock, lock_flags);
 		phys_enc->enable_state = DPU_ENC_ENABLED;
 	}
